## Context and authority

This record replaces [0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) with a review signed using
the course-issued page proof. The classification and triage decision are unchanged.
Accepted records 0001 and 0002 remain byte-for-byte unchanged as history.
The [active triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) points here.

The original [subject-only decision](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) was accepted but
stale: its rendered page warns that nobody has reviewed it for more than half a year.
The incident's "one issue, one fix" prose contradicted the computed cause table.
Read the rendered evidence, not just its Markdown or the word "known".

Scope: the support desk's export dated 4 October 2026, reviewed on 28 October.
Counts below describe that snapshot, not today's queue. Rebuild when data changes.

## Separate problems and tickets

<CauseTable ticket={4471} issues={issueLinks} />

**Parser:** the shared parser reads month first for day-first tenants.
Harbour Dental's app report R-41200 says 7 April became 4 July.
The app/email and booking-v2 form paths must honor the established tenant date contract.
[Parser ticket](https://github.com/manojparvathaneni/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

**Hint:** booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but reads form input using the day-first
tenant convention. A person following the hint gets a different date.
Copper Studio's form report R-41230 describes 6 January becoming 1 June;
intake tagged it `parser`, but it belongs to `hint`.
Align the hint and the form input contract independently of the shared-parser fix.
[Hint ticket](https://github.com/manojparvathaneni/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

The exported cause model is not the production booking implementation.
These tickets specify separate fixes and acceptance checks; neither production fix has
been verified here. Source support ticket #4471 is not an issue number in this repo.

## Count and chronology

<ExportEvidence />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports begin in April. The July merge spike is desk backlog activity, not the onset of a
new problem. Received dates and merged dates answer different questions.
The one-day descriptions remain visible in the computed evidence; they do not establish
an additional timezone cause.

## Decision: merge only established matching causes

1. Deduplicate overlapping export rows by report ID before counting reports.
2. Read the report and resolve its tenant, locale, booking-form version, and channel.
   Do not substitute `meta.intakeTag`, browser locale, or subject text for tenant evidence.
3. Use `dayFirst` and `causeOf` from `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`. For known day-first tenants,
   booking-v3 **form** reports are `hint`; app/email and booking-v2 form reports are `parser`.
4. Merge only when the evidence establishes the same cause. A matching subject is neither
   necessary nor sufficient. `sameCause` covers these known date causes, not every product
   handled by the support desk.
5. Unknown tenant, unsupported locale, or unclear behavior: keep the report separate and
   request evidence. Do not silently classify it as `parser` or merge it on subject alone.

## Check the active rule

<DedupeExplorer />

- Kettle Books app and email reports: different subjects, same parser cause; merge.
- Alder Physio form versus app: same subject, different causes; keep apart.
- Copper Studio form versus Morrow Tax form: same subject, different causes; keep apart.
- Pale Harbour and Alder Physio forms: different subjects, same hint cause; merge.
- Unknown sender: matching subjects do not establish a cause; keep unresolved.

## Consequences

Engineering gets one ticket per cause with its own report count. Triage now requires a
tenant lookup and a reading of the report rather than a subject-only shortcut.
The working desk's triage and incident pages point here, so the old merge rule is not left
as active guidance.

The exported data still contains the original merges. Filing these GitHub tickets does
not rewrite the source ticket system. New reports or tenant changes require a fresh
classification and review; do not mix live queue totals into this dated snapshot.

